<!--ID=B7267351-473F-409D-9765-754A8EBCDE05;Version=1|{"VoiceNameToIdMapItems":[{"Id":"f1b99834-fbfc-4d32-846d-c4dbd3050c19","Name":"Microsoft Server Speech Text to Speech Voice (en-GB, OllieMultilingualNeural)","ShortName":"en-GB-OllieMultilingualNeural","Locale":"en-GB","VoiceType":"StandardVoice"}]}-->
<!--ID=FCB40C2B-1F9F-4C26-B1A1-CF8E67BE07D1;Version=1|{"Files":{}}-->
<!--ID=5B95B1CC-2C7B-494F-B746-CF22A0E779B7;Version=1|{"Locales":{"en-US":{"AutoApplyCustomLexiconFiles":[{}]},"en-GB":{"AutoApplyCustomLexiconFiles":[{}]}}}-->
<speak xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2001/10/synthesis"
       xmlns:mstts="http://www.w3.org/2001/mstts"
       xmlns:emo="http://www.w3.org/2009/10/emotionml"
       version="1.0"
       xml:lang="en-GB">
  <voice name="en-GB-OllieMultilingualNeural">
    <prosody rate="-11.25%" pitch="-2.90%">
      As the ark rose, it would have taken time.<break time="500ms"/>
      Not a single day of work, but many ordinary days.<break time="500ms"/>
      Boards shaped and set into place.<break time="500ms"/>
      Measurements checked, and checked again.<break time="1800ms"/>

      Imagine the sound of tools.<break time="500ms"/>
      The steady strike, and the scrape of wood.<break time="500ms"/>
      The patient building of rooms within the ark.<break time="1000ms"/>
      Spaces for rest.<break time="500ms"/>
      Spaces for food.<break time="500ms"/>
      Spaces for living creatures to be kept safe.<break time="1800ms"/>

      Genesis speaks of covering the ark with pitch.<break time="500ms"/>
      A simple, practical sealing.<break time="500ms"/>
      So the waters would stay outside, and life would stay within.<break time="1800ms"/>

      Noah and his family would have gathered supplies.<break time="500ms"/>
      Grain and dried food.<break time="500ms"/>
      Water stored carefully.<break time="500ms"/>
      Simple provisions for long days.<break time="1800ms"/>

      None of it was dramatic.<break time="500ms"/>
      It was steady preparation.<break time="1800ms"/>

      A shelter is built by small faithful actions.<break time="1000ms"/>
      God is not hurried in His care.<break time="1000ms"/>
      You can do less than you think, and still be held.<break time="1800ms"/>
      You can rest.<break time="3800ms"/>
    </prosody>
  </voice>
</speak>
